node_modules/
# office.db and world.db are pure indexes — delete either at any moment and lose
# nothing. dynamic.db is NOT: it is store-canon, and deleting it costs every
# entity position and attachment since the last crossing-save, plus whatever
# speech has not yet been crystallized. `npm run dynamic:rebuild` is the way back.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
office-keys.json
town-clone/
# the world clone the box actually serves from: `WORLD_CLONE`, else
# `office/world-clone`, else `../postmark-world` (src/world.mjs). Its sibling
# `town-clone/` has been ignored since the beginning and this one never was —
# so on the box, and in any dev worktree that reaches its clone through a link,
# an entire second repository sits untracked in `git status` waiting to be
# swept into a commit by `git add -A`.
world-clone/
world-clone-pool/
draft-locks/
server.log
telemetry/access-*.jsonl
voices-log.jsonl*
# the world store's shadow diffs: an operator's soak record, rebuildable by
# running the shadow again (WORLD_STORE_SHADOW=1)
world-shadow-diff.jsonl*
# the world store's window: regenerated at the end of every hydration, ~850 KiB
# each, and rebuildable from world.db at any moment
*.gexf
.probe/
